title: Proposition 14
---
order: 14
---
short_label: XI.14
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: Planes to which the same straight line is at right angles are parallel.
----
proof:

Let any straight line {AB} be at right angles to each of the planes {CD} and {EF}.

I say that the planes are parallel.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="310" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="XI.14 diagram" src="propXI14.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Joyce's figure: the planes CD (P, through A) and EF (Q, through B),
    // the line AB at right angles to both, and off to the right the
    // supposed common section GH with K on it, joined to A and B.
    //
    // Added, all transparent: CD and EF, faceless twins of the filled
    // planes P and Q (a filled polygon is raised over the figure when
    // highlighted, #140), named as the prose names the planes; ABK, the
    // triangle; and the right-angle squares at B and A for ABK and BAK,
    // right by XI.Def.3 within the reductio. The supposition (GH, K, AK,
    // BK) is withdrawn on the closing slides once the planes are shown
    // not to meet.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): X, Y, Z, C, D, E, F, A, G
    // free; B, H, K sliders. G, H and K arrive with the supposition, so
    // they are deferred. C1, D1, E1, F1 are derived and listed per slide.
    var GIVEN = ["P","Q","CD","EF","C","D","E","F","C1","D1","E1","F1",
                 "A","B","AB"];
    var SECT  = GIVEN.concat(["G","H","GH"]);
