            { text: "For the same reason the angle {BAK|angBAK} is also right.",
              visible: JOIN.concat(["angABK","angBAK"]),
              highlighted: ["AK","CD","angBAK"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "angBAK", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "Thus, in the triangle {ABK} the sum of the two angles {ABK|angABK} and {BAK|angBAK} equals two right angles,",
              visible: JOIN.concat(["ABK","angABK","angBAK"]),
              highlighted: ["ABK","angABK","angBAK"] },
            { text: "which is impossible.",
              visible: JOIN.concat(["ABK","angABK","angBAK"]),
              highlighted: ["ABK"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "two angles of a triangle are less than two right angles", ref: "I.17" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the planes {CD} and {EF} do not meet when produced.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["CD","EF"] },
            { text: "Therefore the planes {CD} and {EF} are parallel.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["CD","EF"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "planes which do not meet", ref: "XI.Def.8" }] },
            { text: "Therefore, planes at right angles to the same straight line are parallel.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB","CD","EF"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "XI.14") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "I.17":     "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI17/",
        "XI.Def.3": "/elements/books/bookXI/definitions/defXI3/",
        "XI.Def.8": "/elements/books/bookXI/definitions/defXI8/",
        "XI.3":     "/elements/books/bookXI/propositions/propXI3/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

For, if not, then they meet when produced. Let them meet. Then they intersect as a straight line. Let it be {GH}. [!just XI.Def.8, XI.3]

Take a point {K} at random on {GH}, and join {AK} and {BK}.

Now, since {AB} is at right angles to the plane {EF}, therefore {AB} is also at right angle to {BK} which is a straight line in the plane {EF} produced. Therefore the angle {ABK|angABK} is right. For the same reason the angle {BAK|angBAK} is also right. [!just XI.Def.3]

Thus, in the triangle {ABK} the sum of the two angles {ABK|angABK} and {BAK|angBAK} equals two right angles, which is impossible. [!just I.17]

Therefore the planes {CD} and {EF} do not meet when produced. Therefore the planes {CD} and {EF} are parallel. [!just XI.Def.8]

Therefore, *planes at right angles to the same straight line are parallel.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
----
guide:

Part of this proof is unnecessary. The line {GH} is irrelevant. If the two points meet, then they meet at some point, so the point {K} might just as well be taken as a point where they meet. The proof should, however, include another case, and that is where the given line meets both given planes at a point common to both planes.

#### Use of this proposition

This proposition is used in the proof of the next one.
